{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.Flat2D","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.FlatTransport"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.exists_eq_mul_of_isSol2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.exists_eq_mul_of_isSol2","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L198-L218","doc":"**Uniqueness.** On an open rectangle, a solution `S` of the two-variable system is a\nconstant right multiple of a pointwise invertible solution `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.eq_of_hasDerivAt_zero_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.eq_of_hasDerivAt_zero_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L191-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.hasDerivAt_inverse_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.hasDerivAt_inverse_mul","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L176-L188","doc":"If `f' = Ω f`, `g' = Ω g` at `x` and `f x` is a unit, then `f⁻¹ g` is stationary at `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.exists_reference2_isSol2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.exists_reference2_isSol2","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L159-L172","doc":"`exists_reference2` in the form of `IsSol2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.exists_reference2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.exists_reference2","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L135-L157","doc":"**Reference solution.** A flat connection `fa da + fb db` (continuous derivatives) on an\nopen domain star-shaped about `c` has a fundamental solution `N`, `dN = (fa da + fb db) N`,\ninvertible on `D` and with `N c = 1` (radial transport). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.isFlatOn_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.isFlatOn_form","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L113-L133","doc":"Flatness of the two-component form reduces to the single `(1,0),(0,1)` identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.clm_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.clm_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L106-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.form_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.form_eq","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L102-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.sR2_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.sR2_apply","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Flat2D.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Flat2D.sR1_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Flat2D.sR1_apply","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103c